0.07: Fix saveData() so files are actually findable, plus ghost-file cleanup (2026-08-06)
- CRITICAL FIX: saveData() used Storage.open()/StorageFile (chunked writes)
  instead of a plain Storage.write(). Espruino appends a raw chunk-number
  byte as the last character of a StorageFile's stored name, which broke
  every `.csv$`-anchored regex in this app (watch's own status menu,
  deleteAllData(), and the phone's file-sync request) - files were written
  successfully and permanently consumed flash, but Storage.list() could
  never find them, so nothing was ever synced to the phone or erased from
  the watch. This is why "Data Files" always showed 0 even as "Total
  Records" kept climbing. saveData() now does a single plain
  Storage.write(filename, csvText) - per-flush data is at most ~300 rows
  (~12KB), comfortably within one write, no chunking needed
- NEW: one-time migration (cleanupGhostStorageFiles(), runs automatically
  on first load of this version, gated by a pulsewatch.json flag) finds and
  erases pre-fix StorageFile ghost chunks left behind by the bug above
- FIXED: deleteAllData() had the same list() blind spot - "delete all" now
  actually erases StorageFile ghost chunks too, not just plain files
- Runtime console now logs "PulseWatch vX.XX loaded" on every load, so the
  BLE console/log immediately shows which firmware version is actually
  running on the watch - this exact question ate significant debugging
  time this session
- Removed a few leftover confused debugging comments in app.js/boot.js/
  lib.js and a genuinely-unused `storageFile` variable

0.06: Remove live BLE streaming, file-sync is now the only data path (2026-08-05)
- REMOVED: liveBuffer/flushLiveBuffer/liveFlushTimer and the 15s batched
  BLE transmission in exports.start()/stop()/reload()
- Live streaming wasn't load-bearing for the phone's risk-score pipeline
  and added a second code path (plus a live-vs-file-sync disambiguation
  hack on the phone side, since the two were byte-identical in shape)
- dataBuffer (the 5-minute flash-backed buffer written by saveData()) is
  unaffected - the watch keeps recording to pw*.csv exactly as before,
  the phone now only ever receives data through the existing file-sync
  flow
- FIXED: app-icon.js had broken syntax (";" instead of ":" in the image
  descriptor object) - would have thrown on the watch if ever loaded
- Wired app-icon.js in as the actual launcher icon: metadata.json now
  evaluates it into a "pulsewatch.img" storage entry, and "icon":"app.png"
  is set for the App Loader listing thumbnail. Previously neither was
  referenced anywhere, so the app installed and ran with no icon
- metadata.json storage now lists 5 files instead of 4 - when using
  "Install App from Files", app-icon.js must be selected alongside
  app.js, lib.js, boot.js, widget.js, and metadata.json, or the icon
  entry will be uploaded with no content

0.05: Persist recording flag on start()/stop() (2026-07-25)
- FIXED: exports.start()/stop() now write recording:true/false to
  pulsewatch.json, not just the in-memory isRecording flag
- Previously only the watch's own menu toggle persisted this, so recording
  triggered remotely by the phone (BLE auto-start on connect) never lit the
  widget's green recording dot, and never auto-resumed after a watch reboot
  mid-session (boot.js/widget.js only resume based on this persisted flag)

0.04: Fix Timestamp Format + Database Migration (2025-01-12)
- CRITICAL FIX: Timestamps now integers (Math.floor) instead of floats with decimals
- Fixes parsing error: "FormatException: Invalid radix-10 number" in Flutter app
- All Date.now() calls now wrapped with Math.floor() to ensure integer timestamps
- Flutter database migration added: v1→v2 adds confidence column to existing databases
- This fixes "table heart_rate has no column named confidence" SQL error
- No app reinstall needed - migration runs automatically on first launch

0.03: BLE Fix + App Loader Compatibility (2025-01-12)
- FIXED: BLE transmission now uses Bluetooth.println() instead of NRF.send()
- Now sends data via proper Nordic UART Service (UUID 6e400002/6e400003)
- Live data streaming to Flutter app working
- Added debug logging every 10 readings
- Updated metadata.json for BangleApps App Loader compatibility
- Added data wildcard for CSV files in metadata
- Format: lib.js → "pulsewatch" (no extension) for proper require()

0.02: Added control interface
- App now appears in launcher menu
- View status (recording state, file count, storage used)
- View statistics (detailed info)
- Delete data manually (for testing)
- Toggle recording on/off
- Green dot widget indicator

0.01: Initial release
- Background heart rate monitoring
- Accelerometer data collection
- Automatic 5-minute interval saves (testing)
- Green dot widget indicator
- Silent operation - no user interaction needed
